 "text": "Hi, how are you doing? Then why not try History Cast from National Heritage? It covers thousands of years from Stone Age murder ballrooms to Cold War. They' done episodes on imperial Rome, from gladiators to grieving imperial wives. It's tightly written, with just the right amount of ad libbing by the actors. You can listen from the beginning, or jump ahead if you like. Then why not try The Invention of History? It's only six episodes, and it's about how we found out about the past. You' welcome. Enjoy them both.",
